tasks.details:
Implementation steps:
- Entity: outbox_events(id bigserial PK, content_id UUID, operation varchar(10) ENUM(CREATE,UPDATE,DELETE), created_at timestamptz, processed_at timestamptz null, attempts int default 0, last_error text null). Flyway V7__outbox.sql.
- MeiliSearch setup: on app startup, ensure index exists (e.g., index name "contents"). Configure settings: searchableAttributes [title, body, tags], filterableAttributes [userId, categoryId, tags, createdAt], sortableAttributes [createdAt, updatedAt, view_count]. Consider language settings; rely on Meili's prefix search; tune for Korean by enabling prefix/n-gram behavior via default settings.
- Outbox emission: On content create/update/delete transactions, insert corresponding OutboxEvent. After AI updates tags/summary, emit UPDATE outbox as well.
- Outbox processor: @Scheduled(fixedDelay=3000) with error backoff. For each unprocessed event, build document: { id, userId, categoryId, type, title, body, url (maybe), tags[], createdAt, updatedAt }. Upsert or delete in Meili via SDK. Mark processed_at, capture errors and retry with cap.
- Endpoint: GET /api/search?q=&categoryId=&tag=&from=&to=
  - Build Meili filters: userId = currentUserId AND optional categoryId / tags / createdAt in [from,to].
  - Execute search, map hits to DTO {id, type, title, snippet?, score}.
- Endpoint: GET /api/tags -> SELECT t.name, COUNT(*) usage FROM tags t JOIN content_tags ct ON t.id=ct.tag_id WHERE t.user_id=? GROUP BY t.name ORDER BY usage DESC.
Pseudo-code (emit outbox):
@Transactional
createContent(...) {
  save(content)
  outboxRepo.save(new Event(content.id, CREATE))
}

Processor:
for (e : repo.findUnprocessed(limit)) {
  try { if (e.op==DELETE) meili.delete(e.contentId) else meili.upsert(buildDoc(e.contentId)) ; markProcessed(e) } catch(ex) { e.attempts++; e.last_error=ex.message }
}

- Entities per PRD fields with auditing (createdAt, updatedAt) using @MappedSuperclass.
- Relationships: User 1:N Category; User 1:N Content; Category 1:N Content; Reminder N:1 Content; ShareLink N:1 Content; PasswordResetToken N:1 User.
- Content inheritance strategy: JOINED or SINGLE_TABLE; choose JOINED for clarity.
- Fields:
  - User(id, email unique, password bcrypt, status, lastLoginAt).
  - Category(id, name, owner(User), nullable default category per user). On delete category -> set content.category=null (interpreted as Unclassified).
  - Content(id, type enum {LINK, NOTE, PHOTO}, title, owner(User), category nullable, common description(optional)).
  - Link(url, favicon(optional)). Note(body text). Photo(imageUrl, width, height).
  - Reminder(id, content, remindAt(UTC), status PENDING|SENT, createdBy(User)).
  - ShareLink(id, content, token(unique random), expiresAt nullable, accessCount).
  - PasswordResetToken(id, user, token, expiresAt, used boolean).
- Add indexes: user.email unique, content(owner_id,title), search GIN index if using PostgreSQL full text later.
- Pseudo JPA:
  @Entity class User { @Id @GeneratedValue Long id; @Column(unique=true) String email; String password; }
  @Entity @Inheritance(JOINED) class Content { @Id @GeneratedValue Long id; @Enumerated(EnumType.STRING) ContentType type; String title; @ManyToOne User owner; @ManyToOne Category category; }
  @Entity class Link extends Content { String url; }
  ...

- Implement search service using QueryDSL building predicates on title and text fields (Note.body, Link.url, Photo.imageUrl as fallback).
- Relevance scoring: simple expression (title match weight 2, body/url weight 1) using CASE + POSITION/ILIKE; order by score desc, createdAt desc.
- Pagination parameters page,size; response includes total and items.
- Add DB indexes to support ILIKE search; for PostgreSQL, consider trigram extension (future). For MVP, use ILIKE with limit.
- Pseudo QueryDSL:
  BooleanExpression ownerEq = content.owner.id.eq(userId);
  BooleanExpression titleLike = content.title.ilike("%"+q+"%");
  NumberExpression<Integer> score = Expressions.cases().when(titleLike).then(2).otherwise(0)
    .add(link.url.ilike("%"+q+"%" ).then(1))...;
  query.select(...).from(content).leftJoin(...).where(ownerEq.and(anyLike)).orderBy(score.desc(), content.createdAt.desc());

- Define schema.graphqls under resources/graphql: types Category, Content (interface), Link, Note, Photo; queries: meCategories, meContents(filter, paging).
- Implement DataFetchers/Resolvers using Spring for GraphQL annotations @SchemaMapping, @QueryMapping with security to extract userId.
- Apply pagination arguments and sorting.
- Keep mutations out for now per PRD (REST used for writes).
- Pseudo schema snippet:
  type Query { meContents(keyword:String, type:ContentType, categoryId:ID, page:Int,size:Int): ContentPage }
  interface Content { id:ID!, title:String!, type:ContentType! }
  type Link implements Content { id:ID!, title:String!, type:ContentType!, url:String! }

